  "id": "COMPOUND:19592 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (2R)-2-[(3R,6R)-6-[2-[(4aR,8aS)-1,1,3,6-tetramethyl-4a,7,8,8a-tetrahydro-4H-naphthalen-2-yl]ethyl]-6-methyldioxan-3-yl]propanoic acid, is shown to interact with CX-1 through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target of SNU-387, which is itself a target of ent-Intermedeol and NRF2 activator Geopyxin F. This suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of the NRF2 signaling pathway, potentially influencing CX-1 through this mechanism. Additionally, the compound is also a target of another compound, 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one, which further supports its interaction with CX-1. The evidence indicates that the compound may influence CX-1 through various molecular mechanisms, including interactions with NRF2 and other signaling pathways. The strength of the evidence is consistent across the different pathways, suggesting a potential role for this compound in modulating CX-1 activity.",
